# Measured: this repository had no CODEOWNERS file, so a pull request opened
# against a branch-protected `master` auto-requested no reviewer at all.
# CONTRIBUTING.md has always said every change is reviewed and merged by the
# maintainer, but nothing in the tree made GitHub act on that — a contributor's
# PR could sit with zero reviewers assigned and no signal it had been seen.
#
# One owner, every path, because this is a solo-maintained project. That is the
# entire review bench, and the "Review contract" section of CONTRIBUTING.md now
# says so in words rather than implying a rota that does not exist.
#
# NOT verified from this checkout: whether "Require review from Code Owners" is
# enabled in the repository's branch-protection rules. That is a GitHub setting,
# not a file. Without it this file only *requests* a review; it does not block a
# merge that lacks one. Treat this as routing, not as a control.

